{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774717,"nonce":"bpn9cvuaaGEqvXjWRvzWP5V0Efw=","title":"feat: run detail redesign — DAG/logs/activity, browse inspector, reruns, debug shell","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #29 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/runs-screen-redesign` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-18T17:50:25Z · Merged: 2026-07-18T17:51:19Z\n\n\nA full redesign of the **run detail screen**, its **browse surfaces**, and a new **debug shell** — plus the backend read paths they needed. Everything stays inside Scarab's existing token system (pine/black identity, emerald accent, gold edges, dark terminal panels). Design gallery that seeded this: an internal exploration artifact.\n\nVerified end-to-end on a real Colima cluster (`--executor k8s`): real streamed logs, workspace snapshots, reruns, and both debug modes driven in a browser.\n\n- **DAG (blueprint spine)** — status-ring nodes with live elapsed for running steps and a real duration for finished ones (derived from the event log), orthogonal circuit edges with an animated flow into the running edge, and a `↻×N` retry badge.\n- **Logs (folding)** — fold by step → **attempt**, each group lazy-streams its own SSE. Line-number gutter, level colour, search across the whole run, and a jump-to-first-error button. A retried step folds per attempt so a failed attempt reads in isolation.\n- **Inspector** — Results · Outputs · Artifacts · Workspace tabs. Workspace is a navigable file tree with an inline (line-numbered) file viewer.\n- **Activity (connected rail)** — the durable event log as a real timeline; the fail-`↻`→recover-`✓` retry story reads straight down the rail.\n\n- **Live attach** — shell into a *running* step's Pod; **debug pod** — reproduce a *finished* step in a fresh ephemeral Pod. One toolbar action picks the mode; an xterm terminal bridges keystrokes over a WebSocket.\n\n- **Read paths for the Inspector:** `GET .../steps/{step}/results` (typed step results — the read side the ingest path was missing), read-only CAS-over-HTTP **workspace** browse (`/workspace[/file]`, rejects `..`), and per-step/per-attempt **logs** (`/logs?attempt=`).\n- **Reruns:** `StepStatusDto.attempt_list` (id/started_at/failed/failure) on the payload the screen already polls.\n- **Debug shell:** a `StepAttacher` port (live exec into the step container) and a `DebugLauncher` port (create a throwaway Pod, re-materialize the step's CAS snapshot at `/workspace`, exec-attach, tear down on close), both on the k8s executor; two Administer-gated WebSocket endpoints. axum `ws` feature on.\n\n- Live-attach needs a running step; debug-pod works after the fact. Both are **k8s-only** (the local executor runs no Pods); the debug pod runs as the image's own user (no hardened baseline) so any image boots — a nonroot image is otherwise required under the ADR-0039 `runAsNonRoot` baseline.\n- Exec is gated behind **Administer**; the debug Pod is TTL-bounded and deleted when the socket closes.\n- Not included: log windowing \"load earlier\", workspace file sizes (the CAS `TreeEntry` carries none).\n\n- `crates/scarab-server/tests/browse.rs` (7 hermetic tests): typed results, dir-first workspace listing, file streaming, `..` refusal, no-snapshot, browse-disabled, attempt-scoped logs, attempt_list projection.\n- Full `scarab-server` suite green; OpenAPI drift check green.\n- Live on Colima: streamed logs in the folds, workspace browse + inline file, finished-step durations, live-attach into a running Pod, and debug-pod reproduction (`out.txt`/`sub/inner.txt` re-materialized; Pod deleted on close).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}